WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.777
A dot product gives us a compact way to calculate a weighted combination of values.

00:00:05.777 --> 00:00:11.807
In this example, we have three performance metrics and three corresponding weights.

00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:18.137
The first metric receives fifty percent of the total weight, the second receives twenty percent,

00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:20.777
and the third receives thirty percent.

00:00:20.777 --> 00:00:27.847
N P dot dot multiplies each metric by its matching weight and then adds the products together.

00:00:27.847 --> 00:00:29.102
Click Run and inspect the weighted score.

00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:35.827
This pattern appears in many places: scoring systems, rankings, linear models, recommendation systems,

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:37.097
and neural networks.

00:00:37.097 --> 00:00:44.182
You could calculate the same result manually, but the dot product expresses the mathematical relationship

00:00:44.182 --> 00:00:51.027
directly. One important check is that the values and weights must align correctly.

00:00:51.027 --> 00:00:57.672
If the first weight belongs to the wrong metric, the code may still run but the interpretation will

00:00:57.672 --> 00:01:01.300
be wrong. Numerical correctness also depends on semantic correctness.
